# Docker-only local development

**Default for BetoGo / tma-projects:** run services via root `docker compose`, not on the host.

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| `docker compose up -d --build` from repo root | `npm run dev` in `apps/web-tma` |
| Rebuild client: `docker compose up -d --build web-tma` | Start MySQL/Redis/RabbitMQ via Homebrew |
| Client URL: http://localhost:8080 | Assume host Java/Node for app services |

After frontend changes, follow `git-and-deploy-on-request.mdc` (auto commit + Aliyun deploy; push on user request). Local Docker rebuild only when explicitly needed for verification.

Future `bff-node` and `core-java` will be added to the same `docker-compose.yml`.
